From 4cf94fec6f9a27266de57b560a2b1e0ff509dfde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:02:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rtrafd: latency and loss on their own chart, with a real
 right axis

Reviewer feedback: latency showed only on the history windows, under a
"Latency (right axis)" legend with no right axis. live.json's probe object
carries each probe's sequence number and result (seq, last_us). The Traffic
page draws a Latency & loss card under WAN throughput on every window: round
trip on the left axis (ms), the one-minute loss on the right (%); live it
samples on every poll and holds the last reply until the next probe, on
history a missing reply is a gap. The WAN chart is back to its two traces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c        |  16 ++-
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp | 134 ++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

